        <app loc="31" ana="#app.conjecture"><lem><supplied reason="lost">ⲧⲉ<hi rend="diaeresis">ⲓ</hi> ⲧⲉ</supplied></lem><rdg resp="#edition"><supplied reason="lost">ⲕⲁⲧⲁ</supplied></rdg><note>instead of [ⲧⲉⲓ̈ ⲧⲉ] perhaps [ⲕⲁⲧⲁ]</note></app>
      </listApp>
      </div>
      <div type="commentary">
        <p n="1" ana="#tr.print">The framed manuscript page number ⲗⲁ is printed with a bar above and below as the frame, not as a supralinear stroke. Measured strokes over ⲛ of ⲛϩⲁ (670–682), ⲃ of ⲛⲧⲃⲧ (778–793) and ϥ of ⲙⲡϥ (1181–1193).</p>
        <p n="3" ana="#tr.layout">Line in ekthesis with an enlarged ⲟ inside the restoration [ⲟ].</p>
        <p n="6" ana="#tr.print">The strokes over ϩ of ⲡⲉϥⲣⲱⲭϩ and ⲉⲧⲣⲱⲭϩ are printed obliquely.</p>
        <p n="7" ana="#tr.print">Measured stroke over ϩⲛ (1029–1047, pixel row): ϩ 50 %, ⲛ 60 %, encoded on both.</p>
        <p n="8" ana="#tr.layout">Line in ekthesis with an enlarged ⲟ inside the restoration [ⲟⲩⲛ].</p>
        <p n="8" ana="#tr.reading">The ϣ of ⲕ[ⲉ]ϣ[ⲁ]ⲙⲧ has a separate sublinear dot in its lower bowl (8× zoom; the ϣ of ⲡϣⲁⲣ on the same line has none). All other ϣ on the page were checked at 6× (ll. 2, 3, 4, 5, 7, 15, 16, 18, 19, 20, 21, 31); none has a dot.</p>
        <p n="12" ana="#tr.layout">An enlarged ⲧ begins ⲧϩⲉ.</p>
        <p n="15" ana="#tr.print">Measured stroke over ⲛϥ of ⲛϥϣⲁⲁⲧϥ (714–731, pixel row): ⲛ 57 %, ϥ 58 %, encoded on both.</p>
        <p n="16" ana="#tr.layout">A wide blank (about 70 px), not marked by the editors, stands before the enlarged ⲡ of ⲡⲙⲁϩⲥⲛⲉⲩ.</p>
        <p n="18" ana="#tr.print">The stroke over ⲥ of ⲧⲏⲣⲥ is printed obliquely.</p>
        <p n="19" ana="#tr.layout">A blank about twice the usual word space (757–795), not marked by the editors, stands before ⲡⲥⲁⲡ.</p>
        <p n="20" ana="#tr.print">Measured stroke over ⲛϥ of ⲛϥϩⲱⲡ (764–781, pixel row): ⲛ 53 %, ϥ 58 %, encoded on both.</p>
        <p n="23" ana="#tr.print">The two dots inside the brackets (746, 773) and the three after them (809, 835, 861) are printed at line-centre height.</p>
        <p n="24" ana="#tr.print">Measured stroke over the restored ⲙ at the line start (543–556).</p>
        <p n="25" ana="#tr.print">Separate strokes over ⲛ and ⲙ of ⲛⲙⲙⲁⲅⲓⲁ (1000–1012, 1018–1032). Measured stroke over ⲙⲛ (1148–1168, pixel row): ⲙ 52 %, ⲛ 60 %, encoded on both.</p>
        <p n="26" ana="#tr.print">The stroke over ⲛϥ at the line end (1155–1172, pixel row) covers ⲛ 46 %, ϥ 61 %: encoded on ϥ only.</p>
        <p n="27" ana="#tr.print">Measured stroke over ⲛϥ of ⲛϥϫⲁ[ⲕⲟⲩ] (645–661, pixel row): ⲛ 53 %, ϥ 53 %, encoded on both. The diaeresis stands over the restored ⲓ of [ⲉⲓ̈]. The bar at 761–769 is the top of the bracket after [ⲕⲟⲩ].</p>
        <p n="28" ana="#tr.print">The stroke over ⲙⲛ (823–842, pixel row) covers ⲙ 47 %, ⲛ 53 %: encoded on ⲛ only. A small solid rectangle (x ≈ 1238–1247, y ≈ 1430–1444) stands after ⲙⲡⲙⲁ at the line end; it is not a letter and is not encoded.</p>
        <p n="29" ana="#tr.print">Measured stroke over ⲛϥ at the line end (1222–1240, pixel row): ⲛ 60 %, ϥ 61 %, encoded on both. ⲯ (arms curved up) in the restored [ⲧⲯ].</p>
        <p n="31" ana="#tr.print">The stroke over ⲥ of ⲁⲩϣⲁⲁⲧⲥ is printed obliquely.</p>
        <p n="32" ana="#tr.print">The five dots inside the restoration (543–649) are printed at line-centre height.</p>
        <p n="33" ana="#tr.print">Seven dots inside the brackets (543–702; the second, x ≈ 572, is faint, area 1, but clear at 4×) and one after them (737). Measured stroke over ⲙⲛ (803–823, pixel row): ⲙ 50 %, ⲛ 60 %, encoded on both.</p>
